# The program of a-tag-is-compared-without-the-string-cell-of-its-text.ir: `if (shape.kind === "circle")` in a loop over what JSON.parse made.
# A short string out of JSON.parse is an atom. "circle" is compared in code that runs often, so it is a name of the image: it has one atom, at a place that the image fixes.
# The type of a cell and its flags lie side by side: one comparison says that the value is a string and holds an atom. The pointer of an atom is compared with that address, and that is the answer. Only a string that is no atom is asked for its length and its characters.
# The address is the same in every turn: it is made in front of the loop.
# FORM: AsRead
# OPTIONS: heat=EverythingIsHot disable=pass:InlineCalls image-form=absolute
# RUN: lower-to-b3 optimized loops f1
# REQUIRES: unsanitized-code
# CHECK-LABEL: name="radii" role=Source
# CHECK-LABEL: steps by 1
# CHECK-NOT: = Add({{*}}:StrictEq)
# CHECK: = Load16Z({{*}}offset = 5, {{*}}Reads:JSCell_usefulBytes, {{*}}:StrictEq)
# CHECK-NEXT: = Equal(
# CHECK-NEXT: = Branch(
# CHECK-NOT: = Add({{*}}:StrictEq)
# CHECK: = Load({{*}}offset = 8, {{*}}Reads:JSRopeString_fiber0, {{*}}:StrictEq)
# CHECK-NEXT: = Equal(
# CHECK-NEXT: = Branch(
# CHECK: Reads:StringImpl_length
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop
# PROGRAM-OF: a-tag-is-compared-without-the-string-cell-of-its-text.ir
